&lt;section id="preattentive-perception" class="slide level2"&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preattentive perception&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Occurs automatically (no effort)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Color, shape, angle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Combinations of preattentive features require attention&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unless you double-encode&lt;br /&gt;
(use different features for the same variable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=".increment"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using preattentive features reduces the amount of work your viewer has to expend to understand your chart&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
